{
  "name": "opencl3",
  "description": "A high-level, object-oriented Rust interface for the Khronos OpenCL 3.0 specification, providing idiomatic wrappers for heterogeneous parallel computing. It employs the RAII pattern for automatic resource management of OpenCL objects and supports advanced features like Shared Virtual Memory (SVM) with optional Serde integration. The crate enables fine-grained control over command queues, kernel execution, and event-driven synchronization across diverse hardware including GPUs, CPUs, and FPGAs.",
